      "textEn": "465\n\nThe crime also went away. In this way, he attained the liberation of form and he got the form just like God.\"\n\nSeeing the head fallen, the royal gate shook. Whose mouth is this, people are wondering. 25. Meaning of the word:\n\nShirah—head; Patitam— fallen; Alokyam— seeing; Raj-dwara— at the gate of the palace; Sa-kundalam— with earrings;\nKim— what; Idam— this; Kasya— whose; Va— or; Vaktram— head; Iti— thus; Sanshishire— expressed doubt;\nJanaah— people. Seeing the head adorned with earrings lying at the gate of the palace, all the people present there\nwere astonished. Some of them asked what it was.\" And others said, \"This is a head.\nBut, whose is this?\"\n\nMeaning: Srila Prabhupada writes this way: “When the head of Kashiraj fell inside the city gate,\nthen people gathered there, and they were astonished to see that wonderful object. When they saw\nthat there were earrings in it, they understood that it was the head of a human. They started to guess that\nWhose head could this be?\nSome people thought that this is Krishna's head because Shri Krishna\nwas the enemy of Kashiraj, and they guessed that, whether it is or not, Kashiraj threw his head in the city\nso that people could be pleased by the killing of the enemy. But in the end, it was found out that he\nThe head was not of Krishna but of Kashiraj himself.”\n\nKing, having known the Kashi king, the buffaloes and the sons and relatives. Paurashcha ha hata rajnatha naathiti prarudan. 26. Meaning of the word\n\n[^1]: Rajjah - Of the king; Kashi-patehah - Lord of Kashi; Gyatva - By knowing; Mahishyah - His queens; Putra - His sons;\nBandhvah - And his other relatives; Paurah - Residents of the city; Cha - And; Ha - Alas; Hatah - (We) were killed; Rajan - Hey\nKing (Parikshit); Nath Nath - Hey Nath, Hey Nath; Iti - Thus; Praarudan - Started shouting loudly..\n\n[^2]: Oh king, when those people recognized that this is the head of their king—Kashipati, then his\nqueens, sons, and other relatives, and all the residents of the city exclaimed, \"Alas! We're all dead! Hey Nath, hey\nNath!” Saying that, they started crying."
