      "textEn": "467\n\nWill be fulfilled, the intention is not applied to the non-Brahman. Thus, the wheel, moving in a circular motion, is approached by Krishna. 1. Meaning of the word.\n\nDakshin-agnim—to the south fire; Parichar—you should serve; Brahmanaish—of the Brahmins; Samam—together; Ritvijam—\nto the priest; Abichar-vidhaneen—by the practice of abhichara (rituals performed to kill or harm the enemy);\nSaha—He; Cha—and; Agni—fire; Pramathaish—by the Pramathas (the powerful yogis of Shiva's group who can assume various forms); Vrutah—surrounded; Sadhayishyati—will accomplish; Sankalpam—your intention; Abrahmanyeesh—of the Brahmins' enemy; Prayojitaah—applied; Iti—in this way; Aadeshithah—ordered; tatha—in the same way; chakre—done; krishnaya—against Krishna; abhicharan—with the intention of harming; vratah—one who observes a vow; vrati—one who performs a vow. Shivji said: \"You, along with the Brahmins, while following the orders of the ritual of seduction,\nserve the Adi Purohit Dakshinagni.\"\nThen Dakshinagni, along with many Pramathas, will fulfill your wish.\nIf you direct it against any person who harbors animosity towards Brahmins,\nyou will be able to do so.\" Thus, Adishta Sudakshina firmly observed the rituals and called for an act of treason against Krishna. Meaning: Here it is clearly stated that the powerful Dakshinagni can only be directed against a person who is against Brahmin culture. But Krishna is most favorable to Brahmins\nand is truly following Brahmin culture. Thus, Shivaji\nknew that if Sudakshina used the power of this ritual against Krishna, he himself would die.\nWould die. Then the fire arose, the pot-like form, fearful and terrifying. Taptacimmasikshamshrurangarodhilarochanah. 2>. Dantrogrambhrukutidandakathorasya swajihvaya.\n"
