      "textEn": "468\n\nHot embers were coming out of the burning. His face, with its teeth, terrifying crookedness, and deep eyebrows,\nwas looking extremely frightening. While licking the corners of his mouth with his tongue, this\ndemon was waving his blazing trident. Padbhyam taalapramaanabhyam kampayannavanitalam. Those who are always engaged in the actions of the past, are the ones who burn the doors. 4. Meaning of the word\n\nPadbhyam—with one's feet; Taal—of palm trees; Pramaanabhyam—with measure; Kampayan—shaking; Avani—of the earth;\nTalam—to the surface; Sah—He; Abhyadhavat—running; Vrutah—encircling; Bhuta-preetah—by ghosts; Dwarkam—towards Dwarka;\nPradahan—burning; Dishah—to the directions. This demon, with its long, palm-tree-like legs, carrying ghosts with it, shaking the earth and\nburning the world in all directions, ran towards Dwarka. Tamabicharadahanamayantam Dwarakakasah.\nBeyond that, all the forest fires, like deer. 5. Meaning of the word\n\nTam—that; Abichar—produced by the ritual of immolation; Dahanam—to the fire; Ayanantam—coming near; Dwarka-Okasah—\nDwarkavasi; Vilokya—by seeing; Tatrasu—became frightened; Sarve—all; Van-daha—when a fire breaks out in the forest; Mrigaha—animals;\nYatha—as..\n\nSeeing the demon like fire arising from the ritual of immolation coming near, all the\n\ninhabitants of Dwarka became as frightened as animals become frightened by a wildfire. Akshaiha sabhayam kridantam bhagavantam bhayaturah. Cried out, cried out, the three worlds were burned by the fire. 6. Meaning of the word\n\nAkshaih - from Chausar; Sabhayaam - in the royal court; Kridantam - playing; Bhagavantam - to God; Bhay - from fear; Aturah -\nAngry; Traahi Traahi - protect, protect; Tri - three; Lok - of the worlds; Isha - Hey Swami; Vahneah - from fire; Pradahatah - burning;\nPuram - to the city.\nFilled with fear, the bewildered people went to Lord, who was playing Chaupar in the royal court at that time,\n\nCrying, they said, \"O Lord of the three worlds, protect us from this fire that is burning the city! Be protected!\""
